      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study was made of changes in the content of natural antibodies (N-AB) to thrombin and alpha 2-macroglobulin in patients with angina pectoris under the influence of plasma perfusion. The content of N-AB being increased, plasma perfusion makes it possible to reduce their content to normal. Provided the content of N-AB is initially normal, plasma perfusion does not produce any changes in their level. In 78% of the patients, a beneficial clinical effect was attained, being more pronounced in initially high content of N-AB."},
